-- call" picks are applied: Photographer and Videographer stay separate, Lechon
-- stays apart from Catering, everything else merges). The rows below are that
-- file, compacted by a generator — the JSON is the source, this is its copy.
--
-- WHAT THIS DOES, IN ORDER (one transaction — the DO block):
--   1. Refuses to run unless both merge mechanisms exist
--      (merge_service_category 20271316823071, merge_canonical_service
--      20271319952573).
--   2. RE-TILES each map trade (source and survivor) onto its approved category
--      — some categories split (Outdoor → Chairs & tents / Lights & sound /
--      Coordinator), so moving tiles wholesale is not enough.
--   3. MERGES each disappearing category into its destination through
--      merge_service_category — every tile holder moves, including the
--      couples' suppliers on running events (event_vendors.category_key).
--   4. RETIRES the hidden "Everything else" category (status only — it is
--      already hidden, holds no trade, and gets NO forward; see the note there).
--   5. RENAMES each surviving category to its approved label.
--   6. Gives every surviving trade a schema row (the vendor_service_attributes
--      FK is RESTRICT) and its approved display name.
--   7. Writes the absorbed names as ONE filter facet per survivor
--      (canonical_service_schemas.category_specific_attributes + filter_facets).
--   8. TAGS every shop that held an absorbed trade with that facet value in
--      vendor_service_attributes, folding the absorbed trade's own attribute
--      row in first (the merge would otherwise drop it as a collision) —
--      then calls merge_canonical_service, which moves every trade holder.
--
-- NEVER: merges a Setnayan product (the 10 `s` rows are skipped everywhere —
-- including `pabati`, which carries a supplier coverage row and is flagged in
-- the PR rather than changed); hard-deletes a trade or a category (both leave
-- tombstones that forward old keys).
--
-- IDEMPOTENT: a trade already merged, a category already merged, a facet value
-- already present, a schema row already there — each is skipped, so a second
-- run changes nothing. The run summary is left in the session setting
-- `setnayan.taxonomy_merge_2026_11_06` (read by the db test; harmless in prod).

